From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:47:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: iOS: a miss under a kept directory listing costs one
 stat

Wine-unix 0208 keeps directory listings for case-insensitive lookups,
but a lookup that misses still pays for the path. The whole-path stat
misses; when an earlier component is missing too, the walk stats each
existing component from the drive root, then the directory and the
reparse point's name, twice each: 11 stats for "Documents/My
Games/Borderlands 2/Engine/..." when "Engine" is missing, 3 for a
missing file in a directory that exists. On the phone a stat costs
45-50 us through the sandbox (those two took 529 and 140 us), so
Borderlands 2's DLC install, which probes such paths about 24,000 times
every 10 s, spent 9.3 to 9.7 s of each 10 s in lookups, with every
listing it searched kept.

- A listing read through an absolute path is also kept under that path,
  byte for byte as the walk had it; a listing read through a directory
  handle gets the absolute path that next finds it.
- Before its whole-path stat, a lookup through an absolute path looks
  for the deepest prefix of its path that is a kept listing's path, as
  spelled. When that listing holds neither the next component nor its
  reparse point "name?", in any case, the walk would stop there: each
  earlier component exists as spelled, so the walk finds it by its exact
  stat, and then searches that directory in vain. One stat of the prefix
  proves the listing is still that directory's; the lookup then fails as
  the walk would, OBJECT_PATH_NOT_FOUND for a missing directory on the
  way and OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND for a missing last component that is
  opened, with the name cut at that directory. Anything else is left to
  the walk as before: a component that is there in some case, a path
  spelled in another case, an 8.3 short name, a name that is not ASCII
  (the volume finds either Unicode normalization by its exact stat), a
  changed or moved directory (dropped), a trailing backslash, or a
  missing last component to be created.
- The cache keeps up to 1024 listings (was 64, full with 66 to 76
  evicted during the DLC install, while it held 285-634 KiB of 24 MiB),
  found by inode and by path through hash chains.
- [file-miss] counts the misses answered by path.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: PLA-879 (owner log pla844/owner-bl2g on IPA 868b7664: [file-miss] every 10 s of the DLC install, 23,188-24,681 slow lookups, almost all not found, 9.3-9.7 s; "My Games/Borderlands 2" missing "Engine" 529-537 us each, "Gearbox" missing "Localization" 426-432 us, "Engine/Localization/INT" 138-140 us; cache 64 dirs, 602 KiB); tools/tests/test_dircase_ios.py (ios_dircase.h alone, and lookup_unix_name with this file.c over a real directory tree: a miss under a kept directory costs one stat, a hit the whole-path stat alone)
Offered-upstream: no; it builds on 0208's cache, which is iOS-only
